+DM_COOP	player	Link Play between our builds (hle_coop_*.c): `auto` hosts on the LAN while the game hosts and finds LAN hosts with DNS-SD while it scans; `join:<IPv4>[:<port>]` joins one host by address (loopback, RFC 1918 or 169.254 only, any address with `DM_COOP_INTERNET=1`; port 47600 by default); `host:<port>` hosts on 127.0.0.1 only; `off` (the default) keeps Link Play offline. The launcher's "Link Play on this network" switch sets `auto` / `off`
+DM_COOP_DISCOVERY	switch	`0` turns DNS-SD off under `DM_COOP=auto` (no advertising, no browsing): visitors join by address
+DM_COOP_INTERACT	player	`1` turns on "Interact everywhere" (the launcher's switch, experimental): in Link Play the story areas, where the game forces Spectator Mode, give players the permissions Palette Town gives with Spectator Mode off (hle_coop_interact.c, at an observation gate the profile places on 2.0.1). Every player in a session needs the same setting: it is part of the mods fingerprint. Off by default
+DM_COOP_INTERNET	player	`1` turns on internet play (the launcher's "Internet play"): links from any address, each proving `DM_COOP_ROOM`, every message tagged against changes (not encrypted); `join:` takes public addresses. Off by default
+DM_COOP_JOIN	player	`<IPv4>[:<port>]`: with `DM_COOP=auto`, joins that host instead of finding hosts with DNS-SD (as `DM_COOP=join:` does; a public address needs `DM_COOP_INTERNET=1`). The launcher's "Join address"; empty by default
+DM_COOP_RELAY	player	`<IPv4>[:<port>]` (port 47610 by default): with `DM_COOP_INTERNET=1` and `DM_COOP=auto`, a relay players run themselves (windows-native tools/coop-relay): hosting opens the room there, scanning asks it for the room's host. The launcher's "Relay address"; empty by default
+DM_COOP_ROOM	player	The room code, `XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX` (16 letters and digits, 80 bits): with `DM_COOP_INTERNET=1` every link proves it. A visitor needs the host's; a host without one gets a new one each session (in the log). The launcher's "Room code"; empty by default
+DM_COOP_STORY	player	`1` turns on "Story co-op" (the launcher's switch, experimental, windows-native docs/story-coop.md) and with it Interact everywhere: in Link Play a visitor talks to the town's story characters as the host does (hle_coop_interact.c, at an observation gate the profile places on 2.0.1). Story requests still count only for the host. Part of the mods fingerprint; off by default
+DM_COOP_TCP	switch	`1` sends the game's Link Play datagrams over the control link instead of UDP (a TCP-only path such as an SSH tunnel)
+DM_UID	test	`=<32 hex digits>`: the user ID Link Play announces for this instance while `DM_COOP` is set (its node's MAC address derives from it; two instances on one machine); unset, nxnative's constant. The account service keeps its own
 name	class	meaning
 DM_AB	diagnostic	`=<frames>` splits the run into phases of that many frames and alternates every switch set to `ab` (on in the odd phases); logs an `[ab]` line per phase with GPU and frame time and attachment traffic
 DM_ALIAS_SIZE	diagnostic	`=<bytes>` gives the guest an alias region of that size instead of the platform's, which is at least the Switch's 64 GB on the Mac and the profile's `mem_alias` on an iPhone (at least 256 MB, whole host pages; the heap and stacks stay as they are): the profile's value reproduces an iPhone's address space on the Mac, as the NSP script's heap check does; its address region check sets 64 GB (Mac only: an iPhone has no room)
